cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this reading, please cite it as below."
title: "BnF fr. 15573 f. 120, a cipher letter in Mayenne-Forget's Cipher-2 (1586): a first reading"
version: "0.3"
date-released: "2026-10-20"
authors:
  - alias: "Harumi-Matsuba"
repository-code: "https://github.com/Harumi-Matsuba/mayenne1586f120-public"
license: "CC-BY-4.0"
abstract: "Transcription, key and partial reading of the undeciphered cipher letter BnF fr. 15573 f. 120r-v, with Satoshi Tomokiyo's reconstruction of Mayenne-Forget's Cipher-2 and Brett Burford's key; shuffled-key control, calibration on f. 104r, an independent second transcription and a vote of three blind readers. Made with Anthropic's Claude; the transcription has not been checked by a person. Code is MIT-licensed (see LICENSE)."
keywords:
  - cryptography
  - historical ciphers
  - Henri III
  - Mayenne
  - BnF Français 15573
references:
